9. See a Professional Regularly
Home checks are great, but a professional inspection reveals what untrained eyes can't see. Do one every 6 months for an added layer of protection.
10. Do What the Manufacturer Recommends
Each vehicle has a suggested service schedule. Following it closely is one of the simplest forms of preventive car maintenance, and it prevents repairs caused by missed milestones.
